<title>BRAZIL: Sao Paulo Feb unemployment at 14.2 pct - Dieese.</title>
<headline>Sao Paulo Feb unemployment at 14.2 pct - Dieese.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The unemployment rate in Sao Paulo city rose to 14.2 percent in February, up from 13.8 percent in the same month 1996, the Labor Union Statistics Institute (Dieese) reported.</p>
<p>The number of unemployed workers rose to 1.192 million in February, up from 1.138 million in February last year, it said.</p>
<p>February figures also rose against January, when the number of unemployed workers hit 13.9 percent of the workforce, or 1.173 million workers, it added.</p>
<p>((-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248 5415))</p>
